  "$comment": "The famous pirates (docs/design/famous-pirates-and-treasure.md): ten buccaneers of the 1660s, each a captain the world keeps, not a passing traffic pirate. Each sails her own ship ('ship' is her name, 'classId' her class) from her haven with a full crew (at 'morale' in battle), fights by her 'temperament' (combat.json tactics) and attacks only at that temperament's attackOdds x her 'nerve', hunts the lanes to her 'haunts' (ports she lies in wait toward) and starts with 'wealth' gold; she sails with her own 'crew' grade, 'captain' skills (combat.json skill) and 'upgrades', fights by her 'temperament' (her signature: steadfast never runs, slippery runs early, reckless boards at once, disciplined boards only at good odds, gunner stands off and fights with her guns), may fire by her own 'doctrine', and with 'terror' calls on a beaten captain to strike that much sooner; she hunts the player only once the player's ship reaches her 'rung' of the career (rules.rungStrength: the men x (1 + guns / 10) of rungs 2, 3 and 4: an armed brig, a fitted brig, a frigate), so a new career meets her kind only as it grows; she flies her own 'flag' (a field colour, a device and its colour) at sea and in battle. Every ship she takes adds its purse and its cargo at base price to her wealth. Beaten by the player, 'wealthShare' of her wealth goes to the plunder chest and the captain gains 'fame'; beaten by anyone, she keeps 'keeps' of what was left, lies low, and sails again after 'returnDays'. The Top Ten ranks them with the player by wealth. Taken (boarded or struck), she is the captain's prisoner, and the plunder screen settles her: asked about her hoard she gives up one of its 'mapPieces' map pieces (keepsakes, never sold); held for a governor, any governor pays 'bounty' gold for her and his nation's standing rises 'bountyStanding' (she won't sail again until she is handed over, then not for 'returnDays'); set free, the crew's morale rises 'mercyMorale' and she leaves the captain be when she sails again, unless he attacks her.",
